    "interpolation_backup": ["IFRNet"],
    "reason": "RIFE/IFRNet-style warping maps to ONNX GridSample, which RKNN Toolkit 2.3.2 does not lower to an NPU kernel (CustomOperatorLower fallback only), so flow-based interpolation is not deployable on the current board runtime. CAIN (AAAI 2021, MIT) uses only Conv/PixelShuffle/channel-attention and passed the full gate: static-shape ONNX audit, 4e-6 ONNX-vs-PyTorch agreement, 1.3e-3 RKNN-FP16-vs-ONNX agreement on-board, beats-baseline on linear-motion and occlusion-reveal fixtures, and an end-to-end 640x360 30->60 fps board run.",
    "thin_texture_note": "The thin-texture fixture shifts a 16 px periodic line pattern by exactly one period per frame (temporal aliasing), so no interpolation model can beat the copy baseline; CAIN lands within +5% MAE and the gate for that case is treated as a no-regression guard.",
